# Gravelgill Scoundrel: with no other untapped creature of yours the trigger has nothing to tap (CR 609.3) and the Scoundrel stays blockable. On turn 3
# Bot1 attacks with the Scoundrel and an Ornithopter, which attacking taps (it has no vigilance), so only tapped creatures remain, and Bot2's untapped
# Elvish Mystic is not Bot1's to tap. The Mystic blocks the Scoundrel.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Gravelgill Scoundrel
Ornithopter
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gravelgill Scoundrel.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Gravelgill Scoundrel > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot2.Block(Elvish Mystic > Gravelgill Scoundrel)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Gravelgill Scoundrel.Damage = 1
